From da316946329d8039b8cb1336097376c60f08611d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:33:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Material arrays: review of lot L1

Synchronization of the arrays of the materials on the host:
- `solve` synchronizes them before the resolution: with PETSc, the
  behaviours are integrated by the assembly of the residual, without
  `integrate`;
- `PointWiseModel::computeNextState` synchronizes them before the
  integration by MGIS;
- `computeResultantForceOnBoundary` and
  `computeMeanThermodynamicForcesValues` synchronize the selected
  materials for reading;
- the rotated thermodynamic forces and gradients evaluators synchronize
  their material for reading in `check`, and refuse the component by
  component layout (`checkPointByPointLayout`, now exported);
- the post-processings synchronize the materials for reading, keeping
  the copies on the device valid;
- `update` and `revert` synchronize once, in `Material`.
The complete rule is documented: a phase of accesses on the host starts
with the synchronization, and no access on the device may happen during
this phase.

`MaterialArrays`: the arrays are private (no reallocation behind MGIS),
accessed through `getArray`, `ReadWrite`, `Write`; sizes computed with
`std::size_t` (the checks against the range of MFEM could not fail).
`Material::updateMaterialStates` and `revertMaterialStates` use
`mgis::HostFieldOperations`, which copies dense arrays at once (the
generic kernels were 3.5 to 12 times slower on the host);
`MFEMFieldOperations` delegates to it on the host. The synchronizations
called by `noexcept` functions report the exceptions in the context.

PartialQuadratureSpace: number of points counted on 64 bits and checked;
the element numbers are documented as local numbers.

CMake: the library carries its dependency to the runtime of CUDA
(`CUDA::cudart`); the version of MGIS is checked at configuration (field
operations); with MFEM compiled with HIP, the sources containing kernels
of MFEM are left out instead of failing the configuration.

Tests: each entry point (accessors, integration, post-processings,
revert, update) is called after writing all the arrays on the device;
update and revert in both layouts; the six accessors refused in the
component by component layout; a behaviour computing the stored energy;
a material without point; copies and fills of views in both directions
and layouts. Removing the synchronization of the integration, of revert,
of update, of the tangent operator blocks or of an accessor makes the
test fail (debug device, and cuda device where values are compared).
